Adaptation_method:
Do not pass objects with functions or symbols to subprocess.send().
// Before:
subprocess.send({example: true, getExample() {}});
// After:
subprocess.send({example: true});

If you need to send functions or symbols, you must refactor your code so those properties are excluded before sending, or handle them separately. Alternatively, explicitly pass 'serialization: "json"' as an option to revert to the old behavior:
subprocess.send(obj, {serialization: 'json'});
